 "structural_change": "the flat 8-bank tile dsfd_vm_bgr (63,416 sinks on one root, 5,441 feed-through bits over an 8-macro column, GRT 20,000 markers) is replaced by 8 identical one-bank hard leaves dsfd_vm_bgl28, every N/S bit registered at both pin faces (leaf hop 2), one SRAM and one clock root of ~14.5k sinks a leaf, under a wires-only parent",
 "why_floorplan": "wires-only parent of 8 abutted one-bank leaves (8 x 77.76 = 622.08): the N/S buses connect by abutment at the same x / layer per bit, the parent's own nets are ck / rs / grp (W) and the 3-bit bank-index straps",
 "open_points": [
  "ZERO channel area: the 8 leaves fill the outline, so the parent has no row for the bi tie cells or for clock-spine buffers. Either (a) a 21.6 um strap column on the W side (slot 367.2 wide, N/S pin x unchanged, slot change request) or (b) no hardened parent: the 8 leaves are die-placed in the slot, the die delivers ck at each leaf's W pin (die clock rule: phi - R, R = leaf boundary mean 329.8 ps TT) and ties bi / grp.  Decide when the leaf view exists; NOT gated (ref_tile gen reads the child LEF).",
  "slot 345.6 x 622.08 requested in el1011-s81die.log 07:58 (not yet granted)"
 ],
